> > > Artifacts limited by altar:

> > Seems a little harsh to set it all the way down at 20%.
>
> I'm curious as to why low-altar games are hard as the game stands
> right now.

Mostly because it's nice to be able to BUC-ID stuff early game (especially
for those who play petless) and it's nice to be able to sac decently large
monsters late-game for AC.  And it's nice to get at least one decent
weapon before Medusa (my current B has *no* altars, but found Firebrand
lying around.  Were it not for that, I'd have died long ago.)

It's not like low-altar games are really *hard* right now.  They're only
moderately harder than high-altar games (except if you have a =oSD, which
makes high-altar games way easy.)  But this patch will make them quite a
bit more difficult -- if the only sacable altar is the cross-aligned
minetown altar, then there's a good chance you can only get one artifact
weapon, and that it will be a fairly specialized weapon that you might not
want for that class.  So instead of differentiating between classes (your
stated goal) it'll more likely differentiate between high-altar and
low-altar games, which, IMO, we don't need to do more of.

> If you could play every class
> and always end up with <insert my favorite blessed fooproof +7
> artifact here>, then every class ends up being (mostly) the same.

Yes, but of course, if you have to play every class with a blessed
fooproof +7 "I only got one altar all game, so I have to use this artifact
even though it's totally wrong for this character" weapon it's even less
interesting.

You've made a lot of other artifacts useful, in order to give us
interesting choices.  But it's not an interesting choice if I can only
*get* one or two artifacts -- there's barely any choice at all.  I'd like
the freedom to explore all the artifacts available, and pick the one that
goes well with my class and other equipment -- I'd rather not have a
particular artifact forced on me because there's only one altar and I just
can't get another weapon.  Because it's so hard to get artifacts now, you
haven't made it so people will use the weapons because they're interesting
and fit the class well, rather, that they'll use them because they're the
only weapons they can get.  And that is a Bad Thing (TM).

For completeness, I should say that between my wife and I, we have 7
ascensions (4W S M R), 4 others that made the late game (P extinctionist
at 95%, V awaiting Rodney wish-geno-polyself-polypile-pet less, K
temporarily abandoned after BoH accident with Orcus, W savescummed as an
early experiment to see how the late game played), and 2 decent
quest-level characters (W atheist, B).  Between them, they wielded Frosty
thrice, GS twice (once with Vorpy), Magicbane twice, Stormy+daggers,
Excalibur twice (once throwing Mojo, once with a Crysknife), Firebrand,
Aesculapius+Vorpy, and the atheist has yet to find a good weapon.  So I
use a lot of different weapons -- and I'd use a lot more of them if they
are made interesting, which this patch does (would I apply the patch if I
didn't intend to use different weapons?)  I might play a knight with
Dragonslayer, or an archaeologist with Giantslayer, or an Orcish caveman
might use Grimtooth for a while, or whatever.  A barbarian might go with
Trollsbane, at least up until the quest, and a lot of classes would use
Demonbane late game.  But this is only if these classes can get those
artifacts.

Changing the weapons around will add plenty of differentiation between
classes.  Making the weapons hard to get will remove that differentiation.
All the cool balance changes you've done become useless if you can't get
more than 2 artifacts in your average game -- if there's no choice to
make, what does it matter that the weapons are cool?

> Or, perhaps what I'm really saying is that I /don't/ think the classes
> should be balanced and that some should be much easier and some much
