Interesting, but IMO, excessive.  Also, by the time you get Frost Brand in
most games, you're probably trying to *avoid* getting more levels ;)

I really like the concept here... I love some of the artifact
modifications, and I'd play with a lot of them now, though some of the top
ones seem a little over-nerfed.  I'd definitely use the different weapons
now.

But of course the major problem is that there isn't a lot of choice if
you're not able to get multiple artifacts in the first place.

It seems like the patch is trying to do too much at once -- trying to make
the artifacts interesting, and trying to reduce the number you can get,
and trying to add some new punishments for angering various gods.  And
these goals are not necessarily compatible -- I think making the artifacts
interesting should be a patch unto itself, and changing their availability
should be something entirely different.  I'd say anyone using your patch
is already going to be interested in using different weapons -- so there's
not a lot of need to force them to by lowering the number in the game.

I don't mean to sound like an ungrateful whiny lamer or anything -- I
really do appreciate you writing this patch -- but I think, as it stands,
I wouldn't want to use it as a whole.  It takes away too many choices.  It
doesn't make for interesting decisions relating to artifacts, it just
forces them on the player, and that is a Bad Thing (TM).



